# Build output, which is enormous and never belongs in a build context: `rust/target`
# alone is several gigabytes, and Docker uploads the context before it reads the first
# instruction.
#
# Deliberately short. The .NET and React images are built from this same context and have
# worked for years without a list of exclusions; this adds only what the Rust work created.
rust/target/
rust/.run/
rust/crates/*/dist/
